WEBVTT

00:00:00.430 --> 00:00:04.960
Mental models are internal representations of how a system, task, or situation works.

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:07.850
They help performers interpret what they see and decide what to do next.

00:00:07.850 --> 00:00:12.120
A strong mental model connects parts into a working picture: what is normal,

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:15.740
what is unusual, which signals are meaningful, what failure modes are plausible,

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:18.375
and which actions are likely to change the outcome.

00:00:18.375 --> 00:00:21.200
Situational awareness is the practical ability to notice, interpret,

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:23.650
and update understanding of relevant conditions.

00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:25.960
It is not memorizing every possible detail.

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:28.750
It is knowing what matters right now, what has changed, what is uncertain,

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:30.400
and what may happen next.

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:33.870
Expert performers filter noise more effectively because their mental models help them

00:00:33.870 --> 00:00:35.860
recognize meaningful cues earlier.

00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:38.040
This is one reason experts can appear fast.

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:39.760
They are not always skipping analysis.

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:43.000
Often they are using organized knowledge to narrow the problem quickly.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:45.810
They notice a cue, connect it to a pattern, check a constraint,

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:47.920
and anticipate the next risk.

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:49.715
That speed is useful when it is grounded in evidence.

00:00:49.715 --> 00:00:53.790
It becomes dangerous if the performer stops updating when new information contradicts the

00:00:53.790 --> 00:00:54.610
first pattern.

00:00:54.610 --> 00:00:56.455
Strong performance requires active updating.

00:00:56.455 --> 00:01:00.075
Assumptions should be treated as working hypotheses, not permanent facts.

00:01:00.075 --> 00:01:03.440
When the environment changes, expert performers ask what no longer fits,

00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:07.115
what signal is missing, and what evidence would cause a different decision.

00:01:07.115 --> 00:01:09.180
Situational awareness is not a static snapshot.

00:01:09.180 --> 00:01:12.020
It is a living model that gets revised as the work unfolds.
